 and 2011, contributing to the understanding of the syndrome.", "TIMIDINA:Thymidine is a nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE due to the deficiency of thymidine phosphorylase.", "DEOXIURIDINA:Deoxyuridine is another nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE, indicating a metabolic disturbance.", "ALHAMIA PRISON:Alhamia Prison is a facility mentioned in the context of MNGIE, although not directly related to the syndrome itself.", "NEUROLOGICAL SYMPTOMS:Neurological symptoms associated with MNGIE include peripheral neuropathy, ptosis, ophthalmoplegia, and leukoencephalopathy.", "DIGESTIVE SYMPTOMS:Digestive symptoms of MNGIE include gastrointestinal dysmotility, early satiety, nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain.", "CAQUEXIA:CAQUEXIA is a significant medical condition characterized by involuntary weight loss and muscle mass loss. It is particularly prevalent in patients suffering from Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy (MNGIE), where it arises due to severe digestive symptoms. Additionally, cachexia is commonly observed in patients with advanced cancer, notably in those with adenocarcinoma of the pancreas. This condition not only contributes to malnutrition but also poses a considerable risk for further nutritional deficiencies. Overall, cachexia is a critical factor influencing the prognosis of affected individuals, especially in the context of cancer-related illnesses.", "ANALYTICAL FINDINGS:Analytical findings in MNGIE include elevated levels of thymidine and deoxyuridine in plasma, which are characteristic of the disorder.", "NEUROIMAGING FINDINGS:Neuroimaging findings in MNGIE typically show diffuse alterations in white matter, indicative of leukoencephalopathy.", "GENETIC SEQUENCING:Genetic sequencing is performed to identify mutations in the TYMP gene, confirming the diagnosis of MNGIE.", "CHROMOSOME 22Q13.33:", "COENZYME Q 10:Coenzyme Q 10 is an antioxidant and a vital component of the mitochondrial respiratory chain, evaluated for its effects in mitochondrial diseases.", "CREATINE:Creatine is a substance that has been studied for its potential benefits in improving muscle strength in patients with mitochondrial diseases."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}